1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,901
Welcome to Pre-calculus. In this first
lesson, we'll review exactly what a

2
00:00:04,901 --> 00:00:05,696
function is.

3
00:00:06,833 --> 00:00:10,289
A function assigns each input exactly one
output.

4
00:00:10,739 --> 00:00:16,346
The pairs one to four, two to five, three
to four form a function. But if one went

5
00:00:16,346 --> 00:00:18,739
to both four and six, it would not.

6
00:00:19,867 --> 00:00:25,342
On a graph, use the vertical line test. If
any vertical line hits the graph twice, it

7
00:00:25,342 --> 00:00:26,437
isn't a function.

8
00:00:26,887 --> 00:00:32,903
A parabola opening up passes. A sideways
parabola, x equals y squared, fails.

9
00:00:34,033 --> 00:00:40,634
f of x names the output. If f of x equals
x squared minus three x, then f of four is

10
00:00:40,634 --> 00:00:43,463
sixteen minus twelve, which is four.

11
00:00:43,913 --> 00:00:49,388
f of a plus one means replace x with a
plus one everywhere: a squared minus a

12
00:00:49,388 --> 00:00:50,099
minus two.

13
00:00:51,233 --> 00:00:57,013
The domain is every input the function
accepts. Watch for two problems: dividing

14
00:00:57,013 --> 00:00:59,831
by zero, and square roots of negatives.

15
00:01:00,281 --> 00:01:06,117
For one over x minus two, x can't be two.
For the square root of x plus three, x

16
00:01:06,117 --> 00:01:08,451
must be at least negative three.

17
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:12,565
The range is every output the function
produces.

18
00:01:13,015 --> 00:01:18,917
f of x equals x squared plus one has range
y greater than or equal to one, since

19
00:01:18,917 --> 00:01:20,909
squares are never negative.

20
00:01:22,033 --> 00:01:27,751
Your turn. Find the domain of g of x
equals the square root of five minus x.

21
00:01:28,201 --> 00:01:29,737
Pause the video and try it.

22
00:01:30,187 --> 00:01:35,499
Five minus x must be at least zero, so x
is less than or equal to five.

23
00:01:36,633 --> 00:01:41,406
In this lesson, we'll learn to spot
symmetry in a function's graph and in its

24
00:01:41,406 --> 00:01:41,902
formula.

25
00:01:43,033 --> 00:01:48,132
A function is even if f of negative x
equals f of x for every x.

26
00:01:48,582 --> 00:01:53,894
Its graph is a mirror image across the y
axis, like y equals x squared.

27
00:01:55,033 --> 00:01:59,854
A function is odd if f of negative x
equals negative f of x.

28
00:02:00,304 --> 00:02:06,064
Its graph looks the same after a half turn
about the origin, like y equals x cubed.

29
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:13,733
To test, plug in negative x and simplify.
Take f of x equals x to the fourth minus

30
00:02:13,733 --> 00:02:15,008
three x squared.

31
00:02:15,458 --> 00:02:21,626
f of negative x is x to the fourth minus
three x squared, the same thing, so f is

32
00:02:21,626 --> 00:02:22,007
even.

33
00:02:23,133 --> 00:02:26,354
Now g of x equals x cubed plus x squared.

34
00:02:26,804 --> 00:02:33,282
g of negative x is negative x cubed plus x
squared. That's neither g of x nor

35
00:02:33,282 --> 00:02:37,151
negative g of x, so g is neither even nor
odd.

36
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:43,813
Symmetry saves work. Graph half of an even
or odd function, then reflect to get the

37
00:02:43,813 --> 00:02:44,145
rest.

38
00:02:44,595 --> 00:02:50,014
And sine is odd while cosine is even,
facts you'll use all through trigonometry.

39
00:02:51,133 --> 00:02:56,978
Your turn. Is h of x equals x to the fifth
minus two x even, odd, or neither?

40
00:02:57,428 --> 00:02:58,964
Pause the video and try it.

41
00:02:59,414 --> 00:03:06,128
h of negative x equals negative x to the
fifth plus two x, which is negative h of

42
00:03:06,128 --> 00:03:07,372
x. So h is odd.

43
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:13,236
In this lesson, we'll describe where a
graph rises, falls, and turns around.

44
00:03:14,367 --> 00:03:19,807
A function is increasing on an interval if
its graph rises from left to right there,

45
00:03:19,807 --> 00:03:21,556
and decreasing if it falls.

46
00:03:22,006 --> 00:03:25,078
We always describe intervals using x
values.

47
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:32,740
This cubic rises until x equals negative
one, falls until x equals one, then rises

48
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:33,219
again.

49
00:03:33,669 --> 00:03:39,420
So it's increasing on negative infinity to
negative one and on one to infinity, and

50
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:41,775
decreasing on negative one to one.

51
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:48,356
The turning points are relative extrema.
At x equals negative one, there's a

52
00:03:48,356 --> 00:03:50,367
relative maximum, a hilltop.

53
00:03:50,817 --> 00:03:54,209
At x equals one, there's a relative
minimum, a valley.

54
00:03:55,333 --> 00:04:00,241
An absolute maximum is the highest point
on the whole graph, or on a given

55
00:04:00,241 --> 00:04:00,837
interval.

56
00:04:01,287 --> 00:04:06,458
On the interval from negative two to
three, this cubic's absolute max is at the

57
00:04:06,458 --> 00:04:09,927
right end, x equals three, where it
reaches eighteen.

58
00:04:11,067 --> 00:04:17,441
A ball's height is h of t equals negative
sixteen t squared plus thirty two t plus

59
00:04:17,441 --> 00:04:17,829
five.

60
00:04:18,279 --> 00:04:23,910
It increases until t equals one second,
reaches a maximum height of twenty one

61
00:04:23,910 --> 00:04:25,426
feet, then decreases.

62
00:04:26,567 --> 00:04:31,345
Your turn. Where is f of x equals x
squared minus four x increasing?

63
00:04:31,795 --> 00:04:33,331
Pause the video and try it.

64
00:04:33,781 --> 00:04:38,667
The vertex is at x equals two, so f
increases on two to infinity.

65
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:44,451
In this lesson, we'll measure how fast a
function changes over an interval.

66
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:53,063
The average rate of change from x equals a
to x equals b is f of b minus f of a, over

67
00:04:53,063 --> 00:04:53,941
b minus a.

68
00:04:54,391 --> 00:04:58,103
It's the change in output divided by the
change in input.

69
00:04:59,233 --> 00:05:03,617
Geometrically, it's the slope of the
secant line, the line through the two

70
00:05:03,617 --> 00:05:04,801
points on the graph.

71
00:05:05,251 --> 00:05:07,534
That idea leads straight into calculus.

72
00:05:08,667 --> 00:05:14,325
A car's distance after two hours is ninety
miles, and after five hours, two hundred

73
00:05:14,325 --> 00:05:15,280
seventy miles.

74
00:05:15,730 --> 00:05:19,975
The average rate is one eighty over three,
sixty miles per hour.

75
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:25,857
For f of x equals x squared, find the
average rate from one to three.

76
00:05:26,307 --> 00:05:31,619
Nine minus one, over three minus one,
equals four. From three to five, it's

77
00:05:31,619 --> 00:05:36,718
twenty five minus nine over two, which is
eight. The curve gets steeper.

78
00:05:37,867 --> 00:05:41,451
Always attach units: output units per
input unit.

79
00:05:41,901 --> 00:05:45,570
If dollars depend on months, the rate is
in dollars per month.

80
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:52,737
Your turn. Find the average rate of change
of f of x equals x cubed from zero to two.

81
00:05:53,187 --> 00:05:54,723
Pause the video and try it.

82
00:05:55,173 --> 00:05:57,800
Eight minus zero, over two minus zero,
which is four.

83
00:05:59,933 --> 00:06:04,786
In this lesson, we'll apply several
transformations to one graph, in the right

84
00:06:04,786 --> 00:06:05,160
order.

85
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:11,270
Start from y equals a times f of b times x
minus h, plus k.

86
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:17,017
a stretches and reflects vertically, b
stretches and reflects horizontally, h

87
00:06:17,017 --> 00:06:19,080
shifts right, and k shifts up.

88
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:25,331
For a reliable order: horizontal shift,
then stretches and reflections, then

89
00:06:25,331 --> 00:06:26,344
vertical shift.

90
00:06:26,794 --> 00:06:30,783
Think of following x through the formula,
then following the output.

91
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:37,532
Graph y equals negative two times the
square root of x minus one, plus three.

92
00:06:37,982 --> 00:06:43,566
Start at the square root curve. Move right
one, stretch by two, flip it upside down,

93
00:06:43,566 --> 00:06:47,688
then lift it up three. It starts at one,
three and heads down.

94
00:06:48,833 --> 00:06:54,588
Replacing x with negative x reflects
across the y axis. Negating the whole

95
00:06:54,588 --> 00:06:57,388
function reflects across the x axis.

96
00:06:57,838 --> 00:07:00,867
The square root of negative x opens to the
left.

97
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:08,224
A parabola has vertex at negative two,
five, opens down, and is twice as narrow

98
00:07:08,224 --> 00:07:09,957
as y equals x squared.

99
00:07:10,407 --> 00:07:15,996
Its equation is y equals negative two
times x plus two squared, plus five.

100
00:07:17,133 --> 00:07:23,146
Your turn. Describe y equals one half
times the absolute value of x plus four,

101
00:07:23,146 --> 00:07:23,917
minus one.

102
00:07:24,367 --> 00:07:25,903
Pause the video and try it.

103
00:07:26,353 --> 00:07:31,973
Shift left four, compress vertically by
one half, then shift down one. The vertex

104
00:07:31,973 --> 00:07:34,332
is at negative four, negative one.

105
00:07:35,466 --> 00:07:38,794
In this lesson, we'll build new functions
from old ones.

106
00:07:39,933 --> 00:07:44,583
Let f of x equal x squared and g of x
equal x plus three.

107
00:07:45,033 --> 00:07:52,244
f plus g is x squared plus x plus three. f
times g is x cubed plus three x squared.

108
00:07:53,366 --> 00:07:59,966
f over g is x squared over x plus three,
and its domain excludes x equals negative

109
00:07:59,966 --> 00:08:00,449
three.

110
00:08:00,899 --> 00:08:06,680
The domain of a combination is where both
work, minus any zeros of the denominator.

111
00:08:07,799 --> 00:08:14,123
Composition feeds one function into
another. f of g of x means: apply g first,

112
00:08:14,123 --> 00:08:14,690
then f.

113
00:08:15,140 --> 00:08:22,187
f of g of x equals x plus three, squared.
And f of g of two equals f of five, which

114
00:08:22,187 --> 00:08:23,460
is twenty five.

115
00:08:24,599 --> 00:08:28,781
Reverse the order: g of f of x equals x
squared plus three.

116
00:08:29,231 --> 00:08:33,007
That's different, so composition usually
isn't commutative.

117
00:08:34,133 --> 00:08:40,575
We can also break a function apart. h of x
equals the square root of two x minus one.

118
00:08:41,025 --> 00:08:48,476
Take g of x equals two x minus one as the
inside, and f of x equals the square root

119
00:08:48,476 --> 00:08:52,247
of x as the outside. Then h equals f of g.

120
00:08:53,366 --> 00:09:00,232
Your turn. With f of x equals two x minus
one and g of x equals x squared, find g of

121
00:09:00,232 --> 00:09:01,131
f of three.

122
00:09:01,581 --> 00:09:03,117
Pause the video and try it.

123
00:09:03,567 --> 00:09:06,853
f of three is five, and g of five is
twenty five.

124
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:11,968
In this lesson, we'll find functions that
undo other functions.

125
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:17,665
A function is one-to-one if different
inputs always give different outputs.

126
00:09:18,115 --> 00:09:22,318
Only one-to-one functions have inverses
that are also functions.

127
00:09:23,467 --> 00:09:28,903
Use the horizontal line test: if any
horizontal line crosses the graph twice,

128
00:09:28,903 --> 00:09:30,315
it's not one-to-one.

129
00:09:30,765 --> 00:09:35,010
y equals x cubed passes, but y equals x
squared fails.

130
00:09:36,133 --> 00:09:42,921
To find an inverse, swap x and y, then
solve for y. Take f of x equals two x plus

131
00:09:42,921 --> 00:09:44,261
three over five.

132
00:09:44,711 --> 00:09:51,798
Swap: x equals two y plus three over five.
Then five x equals two y plus three, so f

133
00:09:51,798 --> 00:09:55,933
inverse of x equals five x minus three,
over two.

134
00:09:57,067 --> 00:10:01,013
Check by composing: f of f inverse of x
should equal x.

135
00:10:01,463 --> 00:10:06,727
And the graph of an inverse is the
reflection of the original across the line

136
00:10:06,727 --> 00:10:07,479
y equals x.

137
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:13,934
x squared isn't one-to-one, but if we
restrict it to x greater than or equal to

138
00:10:13,934 --> 00:10:14,744
zero, it is.

139
00:10:15,194 --> 00:10:17,626
Then its inverse is the square root of x.

140
00:10:18,767 --> 00:10:23,481
Your turn. Find the inverse of f of x
equals x cubed minus one.

141
00:10:23,931 --> 00:10:25,467
Pause the video and try it.

142
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:32,840
Swap and solve: y cubed equals x plus one,
so f inverse of x equals the cube root of

143
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:33,747
x plus one.

144
00:10:34,867 --> 00:10:40,294
Next time, we start Unit 2, polynomial and
rational functions. If this helped,

145
00:10:40,294 --> 00:10:45,860
subscribe to School Math, Explained, and
turn on notifications so you don't miss

146
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:47,112
it. See you there.

